# Storyboard grid generation (Steve policy)

When Steve asks for a **storyboard grid** (multi-panel contact sheet for video prep):

## Grid spec (default)

| Param | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **Layout** | **2×4** (2 columns, 4 rows = **8 panels**) |
| **Plate aspect** | **8:9** — `(2×16):(4×9)` so each cell crops to **16:9 @ 1920×1080** |
| **Target pixels** | **3840 × 4320** (4K plate) |
| **Count** | **`count: 1` only** — never generate alt1/alt2 for grids |
| **Why** | One grid already delivers many angles; a second full grid wastes time and credits |

## Visual style (locked)

**Always** read and paste:
- `dev/uber-portrait-refs/prompts/storyboard-grid-meworld-style-lock.txt`
- `dev/uber-portrait-refs/prompts/game-engine-stylization-pass.txt`

**MeWorld sculptural CGI** — same family as uber GAME-SCENE gold plates. **NOT** photoreal documentary.

Magnific refs per run:
1. Shipped `public/assets/patient/uber/<slug>-GAME-SCENE.png` (patient + hospital panels)
2. `CHARACTER-MAP` for identity
3. Style gold: `vitiligo-wink-diastema-GAME-SCENE-alt2.png` (pending or public)

## Output path

`dev/uber-portrait-refs/video-pending/<slug>-<scene-slug>-storyboard-2x4-portrait.png`

Do not write A/B suffixes (`-alt1`, `-alt2`) unless Steve explicitly asks for a second grid after rejecting the first.

## Video follow-up

After grid approval → pick hero panel(s) → ComfyUI Kling i2v per `comfyui-video.mdc` (one clip at a time unless Steve asks for batch).
